# Fast-forward workflow (fetch + ff-only)

When the user asks to fast-forward the current branch onto an upstream branch:

- Use the helper script: `./scripts/git-ff-only.sh [upstream]`.
- On Windows PowerShell/CMD/agent shells, launch through Git Bash only:
  - `& "C:\Program Files\Git\bin\bash.exe" -lc './scripts/git-ff-only.sh [upstream]'`

Do not decompose this workflow into multiple ad-hoc shell commands unless explicitly asked to debug the script itself.

Guardrails:

- No rebase.
- No merge commits.
- No push.
- No destructive git commands.
- Stop on first script failure and relay the exact error text.
